From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:21:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 57/60] fix(previews): a picture is recorded under the version
 it was drawn from

A preview render reads the frame's html when it starts (store.renderSource,
a copy), but thumbs.create recorded the version from the frame object it was
handed once the render was done. Edits change that object in place, so an edit
landing while Chromium drew stored the old pixels under the new version, both
in memory and in the version sidecar. The next request naming that version
found them fresh, and the route served them as immutable for a year, until
the frame's next edit. A request that joined a render already running had the
same issue: it answered a newer version with older bytes, marked fresh.

Now the render returns the bytes with the version of the copy it read
(thumbs.Picture), and that version is what is recorded. getImage calls a
render fresh only when it shows the frame as it is when the render finishes
(thumbs.shows); otherwise it still serves the bytes (the best picture there
is), not fresh, so they get the short lifetime, and drops them from its
in-process cache.

Pre-rendering pictures while agents edit (a later patch) makes this race
common, so it goes first.
